Romhack Base: Twilight Princess
Timeline Placement: Not too long after Twilight Princess
Length: Medium-Short
Significance: Merely revisiting characters and places for fun (though there is a concern about teaching bad floodwater safety)

Synopsis:
Excessive rainfall leaves many areas of Hyrule flooded, and fish populations increase to fill the new lakes and rivers. New fish are discovered.
To keep feelings positive, a country-wide fishing competition is sponsored by Hyrule Castle. Peoples from all regions participate.
The competition is judged in stages (1 winner per Province) and categories (the biggest single fish, the best at getting rare fish, the most fish by total weight).
[Ordon Province]: Prologue; not part of the competition
- Ordon Village: The pre-existing river through the village has substantially overflooded its banks, putting some houses halfway underwater.
- Ordon Ranch: A potential camp for displaced residents.
[Faron Province]: Competition 1
- Faron's Spirit Spring: A relatively small area, it still spans farther now than before the flooding.
- Faron Woods: The dock over the fog is now the dock over the water. New docks have been built, and canoes have been brought in.
- Forest Temple Glade: Off-limits due to a dangerous waterfall near the temple.
- Faron Field: Previously unreachable ledges have become islands. The bridge itself may be underwater.
[Eldin Province]: Competition 2
- Kakariko Gorge: Dangerously strong currents. Even the bridge is gone again.
- Eldin Field: minimal flooding due to effective drainage, so not a good location for fishing.
- Kakariko Village: A strong current flows through the town, so Zora lifeguards are on duty. The few residents gave permission, so it is a competition location.
- Kakariko Graveyard: Off-limits, as it would be disrespectful.
- Death Mountain & Trail: The water pools gently near the moutain, but the trail is definitely swift-moving water. Gorons complain about cooled hot springs.
- Hidden Village: Only a suitable fishing spot if the entrance is blocked up... but then how would you get in?
[Lanayru Province]: Competition 3
- Castle Town: Like Ordon Village, it is not a competition location, as it would be disrespectful to displaced residents.
Lake Hylia: The obvious location, though now unreasonably deep. Even Lanayru Spirit Spring is completely underwater. Fyer's cannon raft still floats atop.
Hena's Fishing Hole: The other obvious location. Minimal flooding, surprisingly.
Zora's River: Not just the area at the top, but also the whole rapids ride down to Lake Hylia is available for fishing.
Lanayru Fields: Flooded like everywhere else, with rivers in the connecting ravines.
Snowpeak Lake: Might count as part of Lanayru. Not as icy as before.
Winners are calculated after each Province Competition, and at the end an ultimate champion is decided for the entire thing.
[Hyrule Castle Lake]: Competition Winners compete against each other for the grand prize?
Now that could be the end-all-be-all of the game...

...but there is the possibility of a plot.
While the competition is hosted in Hyrule Castle's name, Princess Zelda has been keeping out of pulic eye for some time. In her stead, a minister has been handling affairs.
This same minister might take particular care in banning Link from having a number of his useful items ("for concern about unfair advantage")...
As becomes apparent, the flooding is not entirely natural. Some evil is afoot again, and Link must sniff it out, and soon.
- The final lake has no fish. Instead, you catch a midboss (Twilit Bloat or Deku Toad; if you didn't win a previous competiton, you jump in from the audience to help.)
After defeating it, bosses appear all around Hyrule, blighting each region they appear in.
Consider reusing old bosses:
- Dia Baba: The Poison Boss. Possibly in the Sacred Grove Temple of Time ruin. Makes water in the region toxic.
- Morpheel: The Maelstrom Boss. In Lake Hylia itself, not the temple under it. Fills the lakes and rivers with whirlpools.
- Argorok: The Fogbank Boss. Probably in Eldin Field, though could be in the sky again. Uses fog to ambush you.
- Blizzeta: The Glacier Boss. In Snowpeak Province, possibly the manor. Freezes the region. Potentially has a brainwashed Zelda inside it.
As for the final boss:
- False Minister/Thunderbird: The Lightning Boss. In Hyrule Castle throne room (still under reconstruction, so open-roofed); the second phase drops down to the lake behind the castle.
First phase is probably like an electric wizzrobe. Second phase is more like the original Zelda 2 boss.
The False Minister could create holographic clones of enemies. The boss rematches could be this. Even Phantom Zant from the original game might have been this.
The final challenge of the fishing competition is redone peacefully at the end of the game.

So:
[Prologue]
[Act 1: The Competition (Faron, Eldin, and Lanayru)]
[Optional Act 2: The Bosses (Dia Baba, Morpheel, Argorok, Blizzeta, Thunderbird)]
[Denouement]

[Extra Optional Act 3:
- Fyrus: The Scorching Boss.
- Stallord: The Desert Boss.
- Armogohma: The Cobweb Boss.]

Items & Abilities:
Fishing Rod and Empty Bottles, along with various Lures. Also the Lantern (for night fishing, and maybe moth bait). Also an Anchor (for swift currents; ball&chain?)
If there is a plot, you'll want a lot of things back from your original adventure: iron boots, zora tunic, clawshot, bombs, etc...
A magic meter might make a compelling addition, though it should automatically refill like a stamina meter.
Water Spinner: Used to reach Dia Baba, this spinner glides on top of the water, avoiding poisoned and freezing pools effectively. Can use items while riding?
Pocket Cucco: Gifted to you by the clown duo, you can glide from place to place at will.
Ice Rod: Creates controllable Mini Freezards. Charge it for a big but immobile Freezard (or perhaps a Chilfos? But needs something nearby to make?)
Electric Earring: Used with Zora Tunic to do an electric spin boost attack?

Other Notes:
Hena gives the tutorial.
Malo sells bait. (Fish drop rupees: the rarer the fish, the bigger the rupee.)
King Bulblin might show up to assist Link in battle.
Illia might be Impaz's apprentice.
Skull Kid might challenge you to a fishing duel.
